From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: h265: reject a slice data offset past the slice

data_byte_offset comes from userspace and is not checked against the
slice. A value past the slice makes cedrus_h265_skip_bits() flush up
to 2^31 bits in device_run(), which can run with the media device's
req_queue_mutex held.

Fail the job when the offset is past the end of the slice.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
@@ -452,6 +452,9 @@
 	    num_entry_point_offsets != run->h265.entry_points_count)
 		return -ERANGE;
 
+	if (slice_params->data_byte_offset > slice_bytes)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	log2_max_luma_coding_block_size =
 		sps->log2_min_luma_coding_block_size_minus3 + 3 +
 		sps->log2_diff_max_min_luma_coding_block_size;
